# The town's goldens (port/NOTES.md, Goldens; sonarlib docs/roadmap.md, M6 step 9f4a), written along the town replay,
# tests/town_replay.txt: each scene is the first frame whose keys hold every value its line gives, in hex. retrace is
# vi.c's retraceCount, one a tick; scene the save's scene_no, f the train, 7 the town and 14 the player's house; block
# play's block_table, block_x << 8 | block_z, 0 outside play and in the train and the house. The retrace finds the
# frame, and the scene and the block say the run is where its name says, so a route that changes fails its scenes.
# They are the port's alone, compared with no Dolphin frame until step 9f4c. The scenes on the line below hold the
# game's 2D, which the UI scale reaches, and the others show the world alone (port/tests/town_goldens_test.cmake).
# 2D: train_rover station_talk houses walk_to_house room_dark room_lit nook_job free cedar_shake cherry_shake beach
train_rover retrace=340d scene=f block=0
station retrace=43a8 scene=7 block=301
station_talk retrace=4650 scene=7 block=301
houses retrace=4c90 scene=7 block=301
